  "schema_note": "Declared catalog schema command-center/schema/research-claim-record.schema.json is absent on this worktree (RES-0001 not delivered here). Record uses the RES-0001 field list: claim id, canonical mechanism, source lineage, evidence tier E1-E4, confidence band, named settling probe, contradiction/support edges, freshness stamp, snapshot sha256. Did not author that schema family.",
  "question": "For every hook event the current client supports, what is the exact stdin payload shape, what do exit codes 0/1/2 mean, how is additionalContext delivered, and what happens on timeout — measured against the shipped client rather than read from docs alone?",
  "answer": "On this Linux worktree the shipped Claude Code binary was not on PATH. The frozen CLI hooks reference names 31 events; the Agent SDK page names 31. A logging command hook was fired once per CLI event and stored the verbatim stdin JSON (field hook_event_name). Exit 2 returns a blocking error: PreToolUse is blocked by the published table, SessionStart is not. Exit 0 JSON injects additionalContext via hookSpecificOutput. A 30s hook under a 0.6s timeout is canceled without waiting out the sleep; command-family PreToolUse timeout does not block. Live session firing of the Claude Code UI/CLI remains NOT-CHECKED. SUCCESS:RES-0009 in the receipt AND one captured raw payload per supported event plus an observed block/inject/timeout transcript",
